[37.832374, "o", "Carnegie Mellon University, 2 Duke Kunshan University, 3 Cornell University, 4 Multimodal Art\r\nProjection Community, 5 Renmin University of China, 6 Georgia Institute of Technology\r\n⋆ Corresponding Author.\r\nsinging and speech,” in 2013 Asia-Pacific Signal and Information Processing Association Annual Summit and Conference,\r\nH. Tamaru, S. Takamichi, N. Tanji, and H. Saruwatari, “JVSMuSiC: Japanese multispeaker singing-voice corpus,” arXiv\r\npreprint arXiv:2001.07044, 2020.\r\nR. Huang, F. Chen, Y. Ren, J. Liu, C. Cui, and Z. Zhao, “MultiSinger: Fast multi-singer singing voice vocoder with a largescale corpus,” in Proceedings of the 29th ACM International\r\nConference on Multimedia, ser. MM ’21, 2021, pp. 3945–3954.\r\nY. Wu, Y. Yu, J. Shi, T. Qian, and Q. Jin, “A systematic exploration of joint-training for singing voice synthesis,” arXiv\r\npreprint arXiv:2308.02867, 2023.\r\narXiv preprint arXiv:2401.17230, 2024.\r\n"]
